Make AV1 CUDA decoder tests account for GPUs without AV1 NVDEC support.

NVIDIA A100 (GA100) supports CUDA decoding but does not implement AV1 in
NVDEC. When the default FFmpeg CUDA backend reports this unsupported codec,
verify that the beta CUDA backend falls back to CPU decoding and still
returns the decoded frame on CUDA. Use CPU-decoded AV1 frames as references
for beta-backend comparisons so the tests remain valid on both AV1-capable
and AV1-incapable GPUs.

No affected tests are skipped or deselected.

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT5.6
